      <!-- Asymmetric Editorial Hero + System Spec Ledger -->
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-grid">
          <div>
            <div class="doc-id">Systematic Trading Infrastructure · Unified Research &amp; Execution</div>
            <h1>Research and execution belong in the same system.</h1>
            <p class="hero-thesis">
              In most systematic trading stacks, quantitative research and live execution are separate
              implementations of what should be the same computation. That boundary introduces silent
              training–serving skew, duplicate engineering, and fragile operational glue.
            </p>
            <p class="hero-sub">
              KeronisEngine eliminates that boundary. The same compiled C++20 feature engine that emits
              offline Parquet training panels runs in production—processing live market events, scoring
              in-process ONNX models in under a millisecond, and routing orders across crypto,
              Polymarket, US equities, and custom event venues.
            </p>

            <div class="hero-actions">
              <a href="/architecture/" class="btn btn-primary">Read the Architecture</a>
              <a href="/quickstart/" class="btn btn-outline">Quickstart</a>
              <a href="/strategies/#polymarket-digital-options" class="btn btn-text">Polymarket Example →</a>
            </div>

